<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inner Niger Delta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Niger Inland Delta, inland delta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> is a vast seasonal floodplain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger River</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>. Its fertile land and waterways supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farming, fishing and trade, with cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djenne">Djenné</a>. It was a core economic region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inner-niger-delta.jpg" alt="Inner Niger Delta" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Schmaltz, MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inland_Niger_Delta_2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
